This is neutral translation-quality review of a public-domain historical text. Evaluate
the translation faithfully and apply the same literary standards to every source.

Process the authorized chapters one at a time, in the order above. For each chapter,
read its source and committed file under `chapters/controlled/`, consult the authorized
glossary and inline quality skills, then immediately write all six required outputs before
reading the next chapter. Do not search unrelated project paths, pre-read every chapter,
or narrate a proposed review instead of writing its files.

1. Fidelity review -> `qa/fidelity/<authorized_chapter>.md` (meaning, tone, no add/drop).
2. Readability + imagery review -> `qa/readability/<authorized_chapter>.md` and
   `qa/imagery/<authorized_chapter>.imagery.md` (natural {{ target_lang }}, no metaphor
   collisions, no added drama, no over-compression).
3. Terminology review -> `qa/terminology/<authorized_chapter>.md` (consistency vs
   `glossary/terms.csv`; scan for `forbidden_body_renderings`).
4. Chapter gate -> `qa/gates/<authorized_chapter>.gate.md` with `result: PASS` only when all
   reviews pass. The gate's final non-empty line MUST be exactly the plain line
   `result: PASS`; write no prose, punctuation, or Markdown after it. On PASS, copy the
   controlled chapter to `chapters/final/<authorized_chapter>.md`
   (apply the title policy: produce nav_label / page_title / subtitle). `subtitle` is optional:
   populate it only when the source explicitly has a subtitle or a long source title must be
   decomposed. When the source has only a chapter number and simple title, write an empty
   `subtitle:` and never invent a thematic summary. During repair, remove any existing
   AI/translator-authored explanatory subtitle that is not grounded in the source.

Exit condition: all chapters reviewed, gated PASS, and present in chapters/final/.
Only successful `write_file` calls count as outputs. After the required reads, use
`write_file` immediately for every review, gate, and final chapter. Stop for controller
validation only after every required file exists; do not modify gate or control state.
